{
  "name": "JsonIsAText",
  "comment": "A json value is a text (rulings 1-2). A value carrying Type={text, kind: json} lands as a\ntext whose kind navigates as the \"json\" type. Written in formal so the builder's Type\nchoice (today's baseline keeps `dict` for `as json`) is out of it — the red is the\nruntime's: today the kind of a text is lost or carried as a bare string (`.name` fails).",
  "step": [
